    <statement><p>Determine whether the flux of the vector field 
<m>\vec{F}(\vec{r}) = \vec{r}</m> 
through each surface is positive,
negative, or zero.  
(Recall that <m>\vec{r} = x\vec{i} + y\vec{j} + z\vec{k}</m>.)  
In each case, the orientation
of the surface is indicated by the gray normal 
vector.</p>
<p><CENTER/></p>
